  "Solution": {
    "S": "We have $\\tan 3\\theta = \\cot \\theta = \\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\theta\\right)$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$3\\theta = n\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\theta, \\quad n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$$\n\n$$4\\theta = n\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}$$\n\n$$\\theta = \\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{8}, \\quad n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$$\n\nThus the correct option is A."
